         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/bcbdb4f1-fbbb-4424-88ea-660c844d46be,1795528310104/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C260%2C5000%2C2812%29%3B' alt='a man walks past brightly coloured houses on a residential street' width='620' height='349' title='Houses are pictured in Vancouver, B.C on Thursday April 4, 2024. Mortgage delinquencies are on the rise in Canada, especially in B.C. and Ontario.'/><p>Equifax Canada's third-quarter consumer credit trends report says the national 90-plus day mortgage delinquency rate — defined as missed payments three months in a row — reached 0.32 per cent, the highest since the credit agency started tracking the metric in 2013.</p>]]></description>
